  "narrative": "Using a Bayesian-style update from a franchise-heavy 2026 slate, recent 1B successes, and favorable global conditions, the posterior probability exercises near-certainty. While base-rate limits and market risks temper the upper bound, the evidence collectively supports a 0.98 probability of at least one film crossing $1B before the deadline.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.35,
      "basis": "reference class: baseline annual probability of at least one global $1B film; anchored at 0.35 as the prior before incorporating 2026-specific signals"
